    "fixed-case-6",
    "invariant-7",
    "invariant-8"
  ],
  "routes": [
    "columnar"
  ],
  "open_decisions": [
    "2"
  ],
  "scope": "Settled rejected-transaction atomicity only. The fixture states a conflict that is already rejected at the same owner and effective time, so it does not decide association cardinality, late/multi-writer policy or replay of unresolved associations (decision 2). The WAL assertion compares the segment count before and after the rejected transaction; the absolute count is a property of this fixture's incumbent layout, not a semantic value.",
